{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade","id":1555518,"title":"What lore changes did you LOVE added to Vampire: The Masquerade?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-16T23:36:46-08:00","id":1555518,"title":"What lore changes did you LOVE added to Vampire: The Masquerade?","content":"I know, it's an odd title.<br /> <br /> POSITIVITY?<br /> <br /> But yes, sometimes retcons and changes to the game actually work out really well versus the opposite. Say what you will about Ur-Shulgi but the worst NPC in the history of the gameline was also effective for doing what was a massive boon to the game and that was facilitating the end of the &quot;Murder Cannibal Terrorist&quot; take on the Assamites/Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos have been revised three or four times and each time for the better. So much so that I actually think the 5th Edition versions are the best of them all.<br /> <br /> Same for the Tzimisce as I think there's far more room with &quot;Dragons in Human Form who rule over their feudal apartment building and consider everything in their hordes&quot; than there is with fleshcrafting Necroscope vampires who are just alien and evil because.<br /> <br /> OPP was no stranger to this themselves and I loved how they handled virtually every single plot idea in BJD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T01:20:27-08:00","id":1555522,"title":"","content":"Great examples! <br /> <br /> I liked Revised's idea of one clan leaving the Camarilla while the war for the East Coast was raging. The Gangrel weren't a bad choice to be the clan that goes independent, although the Nosferatu could have interesting as well.<br /> <br /> I got a kick out of Evil Saulot as well, and would even argue that the deconstruction of the saintly figure fills out a story hook that goes as far back as the first Tremere clanbook. The diablerie was never a done deal, and Tremere was depicted as still in an ongoing struggle early on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T01:44:04-08:00","id":1555523,"title":"","content":"I can only read about it in retrospect, but I quite like the handling of souleaters in V20. Obviously it's a retcon, but the discussion in <i>DSotBH</i> actually already read like a paranoid delusion. I mean, if it hadn't given the souleaters stats, I'd have assumed that that was the intention all along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T02:06:14-08:00","id":1555524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555523#post1555523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can only read about it in retrospect, but I quite like the handling of souleaters in V20. Obviously it's a retcon, but the discussion in <i>DSotBH</i> actually already read like a paranoid delusion. I mean, if it hadn't given the souleaters stats, I'd have assumed that that was the intention all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was the retcon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T03:52:20-08:00","id":1555525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555524#post1555524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What was the retcon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Souleaters are described as an undefinable force or collective consciousness, fragment of a spiritual entity (most likely a Bane from the brood of the Eater-of-Souls). The Souleaters are native to the Deep Umbra, and some sources even claim that Vicissitude and Sanguinus were in fact parasitic diseases that originated in the Umbra and were brought to the physical realm by a 4th generation Tzimisce named Andeleon<br /> An infectious spiritual disease that can take over any creature, eat away the body, mind, and soul of the infected individuals until they are consumed and overtaken by it, becoming <i>Souleaters</i> themselves manifesting things that would put Cronenberg to shame<br /> The Souleaters could be the cousins of the <b>Chulorviah - </b>if you want to have some fun<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> V20 introduced the Asakku - Kindred whose souls have been corrupted by excessive use of Vicissitude. The changes inflicted on the Asakku force them onto a new path, the Path of Asakku, which grants its followers Transmutations \u2013 powers that make it easier for the Asakku to learn Vicissitude, convert other Kindred into Asakku, and other abilities<br /> They may call the presence they summon forth a &quot;shadow within&quot; or a &quot;Watcher&quot;, (one being named Aretstikapha) or identify with one of the Qlippothonic demons associated with Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> Same same but different\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 11-17-2025, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T08:09:48-08:00","id":1555530,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> I thought they'd more fully retconned it out as probably a delusion on the Black Hand's part. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T08:14:10-08:00","id":1555531,"title":"","content":"It's been awhile since I read the Black Hand v20 but I thought there was a lot of ambiguity and play options regarding Souleaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T08:20:43-08:00","id":1555532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555531#post1555531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been awhile since I read the Black Hand v20 but I thought there was a lot of ambiguity and play options regarding Souleaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it does. It basically adds a caveat at the end that says this could just be a delusion if you want. That's probably what I was misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T09:02:02-08:00","id":1555533,"title":"","content":"I also loved the V20 Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra and its discussions of Asakku and the True Hand in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T10:12:24-08:00","id":1555539,"title":"","content":"I can't really now remember anything but the already given OP examples, but they're really good.<br /> <br /> With the changes <b>Tzimisce</b> and <b>Assamite</b> went from pointless to be among my favorite clans. I think the same can be said about the <b>Followers of Set</b> as they amassed an increasing number of schisms and deviations and the ones already there became more nuanced. And for all of those, keeping the option for their &quot;classic look&quot; was just as important.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b> I have one disagreement: getting nuked in <i>Revised</i> was both bad and dumb.<br /> <br /> Ok, I have another example, <i>opening up Blood Magic</i>. As interesting as the Pyramid is with their carefully cultivated monopoly, each expansion of sorcery options brought interesting ideas and made the setting more deep and complex. I'm very happy with the form it finally took in <i>Rites of Blood</i> for V20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555522#post1555522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a kick out of Evil Saulot as well, and would even argue that the deconstruction of the saintly figure fills out a story hook that goes as far back as the first Tremere clanbook. The diablerie was never a done deal, and Tremere was depicted as still in an ongoing struggle early on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one I have to disagree, intensely.<br /> <br /> Adding nuance and mystery to a character, especially an Ante, is surely good. But that's not so much what was done to Saulot.<br /> <br /> What was done to him was just to appease the players who didn't liked him because they don't like bright spots in the setting, they want everything grimdark.<br /> <br /> His changes are simple and one-sided, with very little build-up to each one, it's just throwing stuff at the character regardless if they make any sense.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the <b>Salubri</b> and Saulot, just don't use them. Appeasing haters of the concept was among the most stupid things VtM did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T10:28:28-08:00","id":1555541,"title":"","content":"What Black Hand: Guide to Tal'mahe'Ra did was an amazing job. Making sense of all the weird stuff on DSotBH was an impossible task and they pulled it out.<br /> <br /> Beckett Jyhad Diary is also a great resource on canon history for beginners. Those are my two positive entries.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T10:38:00-08:00","id":1555542,"title":"","content":"I love the new Lore of Bloodlines Kiasyd<br /> Loved the old ones too but the new ones with the new approach is awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T11:57:17-08:00","id":1555544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555541#post1555541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Black Hand: Guide to Tal'mahe'Ra did was an amazing job. Making sense of all the weird stuff on DSotBH was an impossible task and they pulled it out.<br /> <br /> Beckett Jyhad Diary is also a great resource on canon history for beginners. Those are my two positive entries.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my favorite change to the Black Hand was one of the most random: the fact the Black Hand was letting the Baali join them. It was such a random and bizarre thing with the fact that Setites and Tremere aren't allowed that it almost certainly confirmed that the Aralu were probably the Baali founders instead of Antediluvians or at least the Tal'mahe're was compromised. However, it's a great moment for the players who want to be part of the Black Hand because it almost certainly is a sign that a car crash is about to happen and there's nothing you can do but bail out. Unfortunately, bailing out will almost certainly get you killed too.<br /> <br /> Basically, it gave a real stakes to being part of the vampire &quot;Inner Illuminati&quot; because you're now aware of it about to go boom.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I liked the idea of the Black Hand becoming a public sect in the Middle East as detailed in BJD. While not intended for 5th Edition, you can argue that the Black Hand is now at war with the True Hand in the Middle East and that is the public face of the Gehenna War. All of those Elders summoned by the Beckoning could be summoned by the Antediluvians but they might also simply be summoned by Ancients of the Black Hand either with their Presence 8 and 9 or Blood Sorcery. <br /> <br /> Michael, the Dracon, and Mary the Black might be some of these new True Hand/Baali behind this doing battle with the Sabbat and Ur-Shulgi's Shepherds with the Ashirra just wondering what the hell is going on and fighting all three sides.<br /> <br /> i haven't read Gehenna War but it certainly provides an actual coherent answer for what the Gehenna War could be without breaking canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T16:11:36-08:00","id":1555559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555544#post1555544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think my favorite change to the Black Hand was one of the most random: the fact the Black Hand was letting the Baali join them. It was such a random and bizarre thing with the fact that Setites and Tremere aren't allowed that it almost certainly confirmed that the Aralu were probably the Baali founders instead of Antediluvians or at least the Tal'mahe're was compromised. However, it's a great moment for the players who want to be part of the Black Hand because it almost certainly is a sign that a car crash is about to happen and there's nothing you can do but bail out. Unfortunately, bailing out will almost certainly get you killed too.<br /> <br /> Basically, it gave a real stakes to being part of the vampire &quot;Inner Illuminati&quot; because you're now aware of it about to go boom.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I liked the idea of the Black Hand becoming a public sect in the Middle East as detailed in BJD. While not intended for 5th Edition, you can argue that the Black Hand is now at war with the True Hand in the Middle East and that is the public face of the Gehenna War. All of those Elders summoned by the Beckoning could be summoned by the Antediluvians but they might also simply be summoned by Ancients of the Black Hand either with their Presence 8 and 9 or Blood Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Michael, the Dracon, and Mary the Black might be some of these new True Hand/Baali behind this doing battle with the Sabbat and Ur-Shulgi's Shepherds with the Ashirra just wondering what the hell is going on and fighting all three sides.<br /> <br /> i haven't read Gehenna War but it certainly provides an actual coherent answer for what the Gehenna War could be without breaking canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree on that one, the molochim Baali in the Tal'mahe'Ra is a rich source of stories and it was really well done by the writers. Now on the subject, the Baali really hate each other. Moloch's line never wanted what Shaitan/Nergal did back in 2nd ed (almost &quot;Open the Way&quot; and the destruction of Thera) and it was one of them who betrayed him (Hay Tau). Then again after Carthage it was Cybele of Shaitan's line who sealed Moloch and Troile. Becoming the most hated and hunted Cainites of them all but also the most proficient in dark lore made a great deal of sense to be recruited by the Tal'mahe'Ra. The introduction of Tanitbaal Sahar back in Road of Sin gave the Baali a different perspective beyond just being &quot;evil&quot;. Gotta add that the Wyrd Sisters (Myranda Kalis, Sarah Roark and Janet Trautvetter) had a site back in the day were they posted amazing stories of their characters before DA Revised. I remember this is where I read about Marcus Justinus Camilus (changed to Titus Venturus in DA revised) before the release of Road of Sin. Sadly I never managed to save it, hope it's still there (&quot;A World lit by fire&quot; IIRC).<br /> <br /> The war between Hands I believe was introduced back in Caine's Chosen: The Black Hand (revised). Kazimir Savostin went to Jalan Aajav after the sect fell to the Smiling Lord's relic nuclear weapons (Ends of Empire). Lets recall that Dastur Anosh wasn't introduced yet, nor the Weeping Master, there was only the weeping stone which was believed to be Zillah.<br /> <br /> On V5's Beckoning I just see it as an excuse to remove the elders until rules were done for them and that still hasn't been published yet as to the why's and how's so we will have to create our own stories around for it.<br /> <br /> ur-Shulgi at war with the Ashirra makes sense, since it was him who purged the Assamites in favor of islam in the first place. I believe that the original idea was to make the methuselah the &quot;third Baali&quot; but that was later dropped from the Clanbook Assamite revised. I just posted on my blog an old entry that was left out that might changed everything if considered canon.<br /> <br /> On Gehenna War, same here, haven't read it so I hope its good because it really needs to explain a lot.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 11-17-2025, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T18:20:00-08:00","id":1555582,"title":"","content":"Some other thoughts I had about lore changes.<br /> <br /> 1. I really liked the implication that <b>Sacha Vykos</b> as we knew them as the serial killing psychopath flesh monster was actually the Dracon influencing Vykos. That was one of the more interesting ideas of Beckett's Jyhad Diary and it's a shame we didn't get to see them afterward. The Signature characters got washed away except for Victoria Ash. But I do think that a lot of the original Vykos assumptions depended on transphobic ideas that I believe OPP recognized.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm going to say that I think making <b>Kevin Jackson</b> Prince of Chicago was a fantastic idea and I liked their take on him for CBN5. Kevin is a guy who was intelligent and powerful enough to fill Lodin's shoes but also someone awful enough that being an antagonist wouldn't be out of the question for PCs yet not SO awful as the PCs couldn't work for them either. It was the same way Lodin was.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm going to give a controversial decision here and state that the <b>Invasion of the Anarch Free States</b> the Kuei-Jin actually was the best thing that could have happened to the Anarchs. Basically, it set up events for Bloodlines and created a lot more enthusiasm for the Anarchs than they'd previously gotten. Plus, it set up LA by Night where the Anarchs have a Council and actually seem to function as a group.<br /> <br /> 4. I'm of mixed feelings with the idea of making the Kuei Jin nonexistent but I do think making it clear the Cainites are throughout Asia and things like Tokyo having a Tzimisce Prince are very good for international gamers. I also do think retaking New York, Mexico City, and probably Montreal were good ideas. Because really...<i>Canada</i> is ruled by the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Boston by Night</b> is a special case too as Matthew Dawkins did a book that reconciled the lore from DARK COLONY to SWANSONG and that is EFFORT for the fanbase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar