ember/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T12:34:07-08:00","id":1555601,"title":"","content":"I think most of the fleshing out of clans was genrally really good. Sabbat on humanity was an excellent idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> While trivial serena the cappadocian surviving filled me with joy and made me way better disposed to the heceta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T15:52:00-08:00","id":1555610,"title":"","content":"I like the 5e changes to the Followers of Set. The Setites were one of my more favorite clans but they were pretty one-note. The whole Ministry split gives them a lot more story potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T16:07:52-08:00","id":1555611,"title":"","content":"Quote not working, again.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>:<br /> <br /> 1. Probably I'll agree if I take a look. Vykos was seriously uninteresting to me before;<br /> <br /> 2. No opinion;<br /> <br /> 3. You're probably right, I just don't think it's enough to make it a good change, and there were other ways to do that to the Anarchs. In fact, we could have mostly the same plot with the Sabbat;<br /> <br /> 4. Mostly agree, even if I think the way Montreal and MC changed hands stupid. Just as Ur-Shulgi, it's a bad plot attached to a much needed change. That said, I'm not of mixed feelings about the Hungry Dead disappearing, this part was stupid and unnecessary;<br /> <br /> 5. No opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T16:17:05-08:00","id":1555612,"title":"","content":"For many years, even back in the days of 2nd Edition, I have thought that the Lasombra would go well with the Camarilla. They have now joined the Camarilla, so I love that change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T17:25:53-08:00","id":1555617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555612#post1555612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For many years, even back in the days of 2nd Edition, I have thought that the Lasombra would go well with the Camarilla. They have now joined the Camarilla, so I love that change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't they already in the Camarilla? I mean, they're the biggest <i>antitribu</i> outside the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I mean, I wholeheartedly agree with the idea, I just don't think it needed a mass migration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T17:42:57-08:00","id":1555618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555617#post1555617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weren't they already in the Camarilla? I mean, they're the biggest <i>antitribu</i> outside the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I mean, I wholeheartedly agree with the idea, I just don't think it needed a mass migration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers are always essentially hand waved but if we had gone with the idea of every clan having 2000 to 3000 members, really you only need a couple of hundred members difference from being a bloodline to becoming a Clan.<br /> <br /> But the games make it clear that the numbers are whatever they want them to be.<br /> <br /> Before the games came out, I didn't have a Lasombra defection at all in my shift to 5E game (that was mostly from the main book and rumor). Instead, the change of the Lasombra from Sabbat to Camarilla was mostly a demographic shift.<br /> <br /> In my home game, the Sabbat Civil War (as detailed in Beckett's Jyhad Diary) resulted in a lot of Lasombra casualties while the Lasombra Antitribu had been steadily rising in numbers due to lack of focus on targeting them as well as the work of Marcus Vitel/Lucius Sejanus behind the scenes. Ironically, the Lasombra also received a big push from the fact they were major factors in the taking back of Sabbat territory in America. With the discovery that the Lasombra Antediluvian was still around by Lucita in BJD, the wind also massively went out of the Sabbat Lasombra's sails. It was also where Lucita defected back from the Lasombra and now was officially on everyone's shit list.<br /> <br /> As such, by 2020, the Antitribu Lasombra had managed to parley themselves a Justicar's position and enough numbers to be about 50% of the clan (technically, it was 40% Sabbat, 40% Camarilla, and 20% Independent).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T17:49:17-08:00","id":1555619,"title":"","content":"Re: The Tzimsice<br /> <br /> I think the Tzimisce have always kind of been out of sync with the rest of the gameline and it was primarily because fans did enjoy gross out enemies that they managed to linger on as much as they do. As Necroscope vampires, the Tzimisce were always treated as &quot;alien&quot; and &quot;weird&quot; in a game that really didn't focus on that save as a function of Paths. Which means that they really weren't any more alien or weird than other Sabbat/Roads. The Soul Eaters, the Eldest, and attempts to make Vicissitude somehow cursed were substituted but the Tzimisce were always just &quot;out there&quot; in a way that didn't work in a game about Humanity vs. The Beast.<br /> <br /> I think there was also the fact that body modification being demonized by the Tzimisce (as a sign of how EVIL and ALIEN) they are also was noticed by a larger chunk of the fandom than people really ever intended, probably due to the queer and counterculture Goth fandom being a larger majority than in other gamelines. Paradox certainly noticed this and we've had quite a few trans characters since then but it was the same thing that happened with Cyberpunk 2020/2070 and cyberpsychosis. Basically, a lot of people really would love Vicissitude in real life.<br /> <br /> The Dragon Tzimisce are just more INTERESTING than their prior selves.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T19:48:17-08:00","id":1555623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555618#post1555618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the games came out, I didn't have a Lasombra defection at all in my shift to 5E game (that was mostly from the main book and rumor). Instead, the change of the Lasombra from Sabbat to Camarilla was mostly a demographic shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this work just fine.<br /> <br /> I mean, who uses the <i>antitribu</i> moniker in everyday parlance anyway? I imagine even if you play under the assumption that Camarilla Lasombra are about 100 or less, there's hardly any reason to not just call them Lasombra most of the time, and that's more than enough Lasombra for most games, as in most of them their worldwide number won't make a difference, only how many you have at your city (which you can handwave as the main Lasombra population in a Camarilla domain if you want, that's not a problem at all).<br /> <br /> Even if you want to play a globetrotting chronicle with high politics you don't need huge numbers more often than not, as the specific demographics of each and every city won't matter. And all it takes for the Camarilla to name a Justicar from any clan or bloodline is for them to see a practical\u00e7 reason in doing so, which has more to do with the political clot of the individual than their clan as a whole.<br /> <br /> And then if you need... just mess with the numbers. Nothing really stops the <i>Antitribu</i> from increasing in numbers, or the &quot;main&quot; clan from shrinking. I think your take was good, and there are many similar ones to get them to be as numerous at each side as you need. And aside the Justicar, nothing else really hangs on a law or something, except <i>maybe</i> the damn moniker if you want it to matter. A Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> can already fill any Camarilla position just as any other vampire, even Primogen. Or any other clan or bloodline, for that matter, except the very, very few who are actively persecuted (and even those can get away in a given city if the stars align).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555619#post1555619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragon Tzimisce are just more INTERESTING than their prior selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think as a concept the Sabbat Tzimisce are interesting, the problem is more that WW never did anything with them except playing the trope at face value again and again. They relied too much on the <i>Necroscope</i> reference, and while it scratches the itch for some players, overall the result was the simplest and most limited clan concept in the game, even compared to old-school Ravnos and Setites (OS Assamite could be argued to be simpler, but they had generic mystery as a creative space for the ST to explore).<br /> <br /> Making the reference even more direct was probably the single worst decision in DSotBH, just because it further cemented those Tzimisce as <i>Necroscope</i> rip-offs and nothing more.<br /> <br /> So I'd argue that salvaging this mess and broadening their conceptual scope is more important to the game at large, so the players can have the OG fleshcraft clan and yet do more with it.<br /> <br /> But that said, I'm a sucker for the Dracula style vampire, and even more the Strahd &quot;I am the land&quot; variety, so I definitely love the Old Clan much more than the standard version. I like both in-Clan sets, but I always prefer to run the actual characters in the Old Clan way.<br /> <br /> And yes, they're the quintessential Vanilla Vampire, but you know what? Vanilla is Vanilla for a reason.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T22:52:18-08:00","id":1555625,"title":"","content":"1. I think <b>Mithras</b> was going to be just sort of footnote in the World of Darkness if not for the fact that Matthew Dawkins managed to make him a character that had a complete arc across multiple editions. Other people used Mithras like Phillipe Boulle in the Victorian Age Vampire trilogy but I believe that the Gentleman Gamer is the guy who really set up the story in BJD that was paid off in <i>Fall of London</i>. Also, the creation of the Cult of Mithras as an actual religious group (and probably Path/Road) in [i}Cults of the Blood Gods[/i]. You may not like <i>Fall of London</i>'s presentation or as a whole but I think that the central premise works very well. Also, the fact that the ending of the game with London as a Camarilla, Mithras Cult, or Second Inquisition victory are all on the players.<br /> <br /> (I'm not sure if this is canon but I also think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> may have been setting up Roger De Camden as the guy behind the Redcoats preparing to take over Boston for the British Camarilla as the ultimate villain of Swansong--its a nice tie in to The Fall of London if you want to do it that way)<br /> <br /> 2. The <b>Web of Knives</b> retcon was mentioned above but it's interesting to really think about the idea of them being a bunch of murderous assholes in-universe and the Road of Blood being sort of a proto-Sabbat of diablerie hungry apocalypse warriors that are really antithetical to the clan as a whole. The <b>Shepherds of Ur-Shulgi</b> have a different name but I like that they exist in 5th Edition because it really does give a very &quot;cheap&quot; enemy that tabletop RPGs sometimes need. They devoted themselves to Ur-Shulgi above all things and now he's just gone. Alamut is gone. So, really, they're a shadow of their former self. I feel like if they hadn't been in Cult of the Blood Gods, a good chunk of the context for the Banu Haqim would have been lost.<br /> <br /> 3. This is going back a long time but I think <b>Justin Achilli </b>deserves some credit for the revising of the <b>Giovanni</b> into the absolutely fucked up and demented take on them that he presented. I remember the original Giovanni felt like Diet Tremere with an Italian bent. Everyone treated them just like mafia and Italian. The expansion into the most personally fucked up family with branches all over the globe really made the Giovanni Chronicles possible. Are the Cappadocians and Hecata better? I mean, yes. There's some issues I have with the Hecata (there's no real need to have gotten rid of the Samedi and Nagaraja) but the clan that had already been rescued from being one note to being one of my favorites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T03:53:36-08:00","id":1555628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555618#post1555618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my home game, the Sabbat Civil War (as detailed in Beckett's Jyhad Diary) resulted in a lot of Lasombra casualties while the Lasombra Antitribu had been steadily rising in numbers due to lack of focus on targeting them as well as the work of Marcus Vitel/Lucius Sejanus behind the scenes. Ironically, the Lasombra also received a big push from the fact they were major factors in the taking back of Sabbat territory in America. With the discovery that the Lasombra Antediluvian was still around by Lucita in BJD, the wind also massively went out of the Sabbat Lasombra's sails. It was also where Lucita defected back from the Lasombra and now was officially on everyone's shit list.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less what I do with the Lasombra in my home game. The Sabbat clan lost a ton of members in the war. The Antitribu had started getting permission to embrace more frequently. in fact the Camarilla itself didn't realize how many Lasombra Antitribu there were and the Inner Council was pretty shocked when they realized that the Camarilla Lasombra now outnumbered those in the Sabbat. Meanwhile as a result of the Sabbat Civil War, some of the surviving Lasombra fled and joined the Camarilla. It wasn'texactly a lot of them, probably not more than three or four dozen but some of them were high ranking and given everything else it was enough for the Camarilla Lasombra to claim that they were now the main clan and that the Sabbat were Antitribu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T08:20:02-08:00","id":1555632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555617#post1555617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weren't they already in the Camarilla? I mean, they're the biggest <i>antitribu</i> outside the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I mean, I wholeheartedly agree with the idea, I just don't think it needed a mass migration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. They were initially portrayed as being extremely rare and having to stay hidden and/or face persecution. As time progressed, the books touched on the idea more. So, of course any Clan could theoretically be in any Sect, but it was depicted as very rare.<br /> <br /> So, I actually don't quite agree with the execution of the Lasombra joining the Camarilla in V5. Personally, I would have just said that there were more Lasombra in the Camarilla than previously thought or depicted and that recently they have growth in number and influence enough to exert their power and demand full Clan status - kind of like what AnubisYx said. <br /> <br /> But the thread is about changes we liked, so since I like adding the Lasombra, I figured I would mention it even if I wouldn't have done it the same way. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T11:50:57-08:00","id":1555638,"title":"","content":"I tend to run the lasombra surge as coming fron ashirra immigration with the kings and queens of shadow defecting to the anarchs. I dislike the defection on a number of levels.<br /> Then again i tend to have cam lasombra as gm approval due to the sheer quantity of bad ones ive seem. One of the harder clans to play imo.<br /> <br /> that said the heceta are easier to wedge into games than giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T17:05:44-08:00","id":1555647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555632#post1555632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thread is about changes we liked, so since I like adding the Lasombra, I figured I would mention it even if I wouldn't have done it the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most of us pointed to changes we didn't quite like the method, but can appreciate the results. I just thought it wasn't so much of a change, but that's that, if it is it is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555638#post1555638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to run the lasombra surge as coming fron ashirra immigration with the kings and queens of shadow defecting to the anarchs. I dislike the defection on a number of levels.<br /> Then again i tend to have cam lasombra as gm approval due to the sheer quantity of bad ones ive seem. One of the harder clans to play imo.<br /> <br /> that said the heceta are easier to wedge into games than giovanni.</div> </div> </div> </div>The defection plot is badly done, that's for sure. But I actually think it makes sense for them to come from the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Simply put, &quot;real&quot; Lasombra are a very poor fit in the sect. While the Tzimisce turned into something that not quite fit, but definitely works, the Lasombra &quot;Ventrue-like&quot; culture makes little sense in there unless you're one of the really successful ones. In the Ashirra they already have a stable place to fit in, I'm not sure if it makes sense for them to switch to the Camarilla in numbers.<br /> <br /> I also as a rule of thumb think the Sabbat should have a large defection rate, precisely because it's a very &quot;love it or die&quot; group. Anyone who stays (and those would still be numerous) would be die hard loyal, if not straight up fanatics, but a lot of people would look for an escape opportunity. And I don't really buy the idea that the Sabbat is so effective at hunting down deserters, that's not easy and they have better things to do. So add the two and I do think Sabbat Lasombra defecting to the Camarilla isn't all that uncommon.<br /> <br /> But not the main source of their numbers, only maybe for older ones. Instead their main source is good old Embrace.<br /> <br /> Hecata are overall a good change to the lineages of Death. I think their unified mechanics is a bad thing, but their lore overall is one of the highlights of V5. And I said previously, while it's kinda strange for all those lines to come together, sacrificing Augustus does the trick for me, not because of any magical shenanigans, but because he <b>is</b> the main source of bad blood between most of them.<br /> <br /> My only complaints are about following <i>Revised</i> footsteps with the Nagaraja and keeping them isolated from their original lore. While DSotBH is bonkers to no end if taken in its entirety, I think a second Mage-related lineage in addition to the Tremere, but with a different relationship with their living colleagues, was a really neat idea (and you can frame them as &quot;witches and wizards&quot; or whatever while in a Vampire-only book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T19:31:12-08:00","id":1555657,"title":"","content":"So, I love Camarilla Lasombra, but I do agree that defection plot had some issues.<br /> <br /> In large part, because it isn\u2019t cool. The Lasombra came to the Camarilla on their knees, humbling themselves. That isn\u2019t their style. That isn\u2019t cool.<br /> <br /> That is why I would rather the Lasombra gain enough power to demand full status within the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 11-19-2025, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T20:13:29-08:00","id":1555661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555657#post1555657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I love Camarilla Lasombra, but I do agree that defection plot had some issues.<br /> <br /> In large part, because it isn\u2019t cool. The Kasombra came to the Camarilla on their knees, humbling themselves. That isn\u2019t their style. That isn\u2019t cool.<br /> <br /> That is why I would rather the Lasombra gain enough power to demand full status within the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>In &quot;The Sacrifice&quot;, I gave the Lasombra an angle to pursue on the subject by saying that the deal they made with Kevin Jackson was very much a &quot;Please don't throw me in the briar patch&quot; sort of thing. They targeted Kevin Jackson because he's anxious to make history and an ancilla so he didn't have the age to spot the trap they were laying but he also was powerful enough in Chicago that he would be able to set the stage for the defections across the rest of America (where the Camarilla, once in the Camarilla, would spread).<br /> <br /> What was the trap? One that Critias spotted but decided to let past?<br /> <br /> Well, Sierra Van Buress dropped the hints and guided Kevin Jackson to demand that the Lasombra present a Lasombra Elder in exchange for every defector. Something so outrageous that it would be assumed the Lasombra would reject out of hand. Agreeing to it would make it seem like the Lasombra was insane and crippling their own clan.<br /> <br /> In truth, it was a calculated bit of theater that came in five parts.<br /> <br /> 1:] The Lasombra made this deal with the assumption they would need to purge the Sabbat traditionalists and loyalists that would not be willing to defect to the Camarilla. The Lasombra were not going to leave a bunch of enemies behind them. Hence they were going to be doing a purge anyway and the ashes could be used to buy their members passage.<br /> <br /> 2:] The Lasombra are quite happy to cheat the Camarilla while the Tremere are at their lowest and the Banu Haqim lack the inherent hatred the Sabbat possess. The Lasombra present a pouch of ashes from an 'elder' that they kept forty bags from, staked members of other clans, false identities for the dead, and lies.<br /> <br /> 3:] Plenty of Princes didn't care about the deal Kevin Jackson made if they received private grauitities. Not every Prince cares about the Sabbat being weakened if they can make their own arrangements. The Amis Noctis cleaned out the Sabbat's coffers (barring the Grimaldi) and can give great tribute.<br /> <br /> 4:] The Lasombra are spreading out or plan to. One or two Lasombra in most major cities is a lot easier to work with than Princes who are worried about an invasion. The Lasombra may not have access to cellphones or the internet...but their ghouls do as do couriers. Their efforts are coordinated with the agents having the goals of making friends and building power bases each city.<br /> <br /> 5:] The Lasombra's final issue is that plenty of the Lasombra just stayed behind when the Sabbat left their cities. Sometimes with amiable ex-Sabbat willing to pass themselves off as Anarchs or Caitiff. Mexico City, Montreal, and other cities have Lasombra welcoming the Camarilla in--its hard to argue with their presence then.<br /> <br /> It was an extremely well-done plan and while it had quite a few hiccups because it turned out the Amis Noctis underestimated how many Lasombra marked for destruction would have their OWN plans to betray their fellows and jump ship (plus take advantage of the opportunity for settling old scores--treachery is the way of the Sith), it overall worked extremely well in moving a few hundred Lasombra and crippling a lot of the Sabbat counteroffensive against the &quot;traitors.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously, this isn't canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T22:37:12-08:00","id":1555668,"title":"","content":"I enjoy the Beckoning addition to the lore as it caused a major shakeup in the Kindred rulership and we saw young and older ancillea of weaker generations get a chance to gain greater power.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel leaving the Camarilla was a good idea in my book and I'm surprised that they stayed as long they did.<br /> <br /> Also it's nice to see the Tzmisce clan moving away from edgelord cruelty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-20-2025, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T22:41:16-08:00","id":1555669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555647#post1555647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The defection plot is badly done, that's for sure. But I actually think it makes sense for them to come from the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Simply put, &quot;real&quot; Lasombra are a very poor fit in the sect. While the Tzimisce turned into something that not quite fit, but definitely works, the Lasombra &quot;Ventrue-like&quot; culture makes little sense in there unless you're one of the really successful ones. In the Ashirra they already have a stable place to fit in, I'm not sure if it makes sense for them to switch to the Camarilla in numbers.<br /> <br /> I also as a rule of thumb think the Sabbat should have a large defection rate, precisely because it's a very &quot;love it or die&quot; group. Anyone who stays (and those would still be numerous) would be die hard loyal, if not straight up fanatics, but a lot of people would look for an escape opportunity. And I don't really buy the idea that the Sabbat is so effective at hunting down deserters, that's not easy and they have better things to do. So add the two and I do think Sabbat Lasombra defecting to the Camarilla isn't all that uncommon.<br /> <br /> But not the main source of their numbers, only maybe for older ones. Instead their main source is good old Embrace.<br /> <br /> Hecata are overall a good change to the lineages of Death. I think their unified mechanics is a bad thing, but their lore overall is one of the highlights of V5. And I said previously, while it's kinda strange for all those lines to come together, sacrificing Augustus does the trick for me, not because of any magical shenanigans, but because he <b>is</b> the main source of bad blood between most of them.<br /> <br /> My only complaints are about following <i>Revised</i> footsteps with the Nagaraja and keeping them isolated from their original lore. While DSotBH is bonkers to no end if taken in its entirety, I think a second Mage-related lineage in addition to the Tremere, but with a different relationship with their living colleagues, was a really neat idea (and you can frame them as &quot;witches and wizards&quot; or whatever while in a Vampire-only book).</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think thats true on a number of levels. I think the lasombra are very very Sabbat both culturally and ideologically. Their are cracks and internal issues but the Sabbat strongly reflects lasombra outlooks (at least in previous editions, 5th sabbats personality is an extensive description of why its a npc zombie/xenomorpth with fangs). I also think the lasombra and ventrue simularities are less prominant than people think.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think with deserters its more an issue of lack of available optertunity, culture vaulderie and &quot;lol no, die&quot;when you arrive being the default options historically. Its a lot easier in 5th because the anarchs are so prevelant and a bit of a joke internally and the sabbat may as well not exist beyond the pack.<br /> <br /> with the ashirra lasombra its more a product of emigration/refugee status due to internal turmoil with vampire society. A little on the nose but it works<br /> <br /> I tend to run heceta as more of an 'agreement' than anything which certain parts if the clan gravitating to differant sects but still being mechanically distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T23:43:58-08:00","id":1555674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555668#post1555668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel leaving the Camarilla was a good idea in my book and I'm surprised that they stayed as long they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main reason they stayed is that they don't have clan-wide organization of any kind, they're fiercely independent individuals as far as clan policy goes.<br /> <br /> And the second side of this is that the Camarilla wasn't so much a group as it was an idea, a way to organize society, and a set of laws meant for every Kindred.<br /> <br /> So for most of the setting's history being Camarilla isn't just default in the sense that it is expected for most groups (actually the default has always been the Anarchs sooner or later in the chronicle), but in the very real sense that being Camarilla isn't an actual effort, <i>leaving it</i> is. Because leaving it means deliberately choosing to ignore it's rule and laws.<br /> <br /> Even most Anarchs weren't necessarily non-Camarilla if they were just against the current Prince or something like that. If you so much as <i>accept</i> that the city has a Prince or Primogen and the Six Traditions, you're Camarilla, that's it. And from their part, the Camarilla doesn't accept members, it <i>assumes</i> it's universal among vampires. While it does have a few global or regional institutions, it was more an idea than an organization.<br /> <br /> Justicars are one of those few institutions, and almost the only one that affects nightly life, and they're a political appointment. So if one Justicar leaves the position... you just appoint a new one, as long as there's a single vampire in the clan who accepts the role, it can be done.<br /> <br /> For the Gangrel being Camarilla was just a matter of other people saying they're in and they having no reason to argue the point, plus there being enough clan members who actually gave a fuck to become Justicars, Primogen and stuff. Leaving was actually a very involved effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T01:33:01-08:00","id":1555677,"title":"","content":"The mention of the fate of Augustus beings to mind another thing that I think went really well, and that's the disposition of a lot of the many elaborate doomsday supervillain schemes among the antediluvians. My preferred headcanon outcome for Gehenna was always one where these very primitive creatures turn out not to be the great schemers that that they're thought to be, and that the world just goes on after they cancel one another out. With Augustus killed by his own clan and its offshoot bloodlines, Alamut and the Vienna Chantry fallen to mortal crusaders tipped off by enemies of the Banu Haqim and Tremere, and the Tzimisce Eldest having apparently found something more interesting to do with the next chapter of its existence than spring out of Manhattan's sewers like a kaiju, I got a lot of my wish. The future's wide open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T05:36:39-08:00","id":1555680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555674#post1555674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main reason they stayed is that they don't have clan-wide organization of any kind, they're fiercely independent individuals as far as clan policy goes.<br /> <br /> And the second side of this is that the Camarilla wasn't so much a group as it was an idea, a way to organize society, and a set of laws meant for every Kindred.<br /> <br /> So for most of the setting's history being Camarilla isn't just default in the sense that it is expected for most groups (actually the default has always been the Anarchs sooner or later in the chronicle), but in the very real sense that being Camarilla isn't an actual effort, <i>leaving it</i> is. Because leaving it means deliberately choosing to ignore it's rule and laws.<br /> <br /> Even most Anarchs weren't necessarily non-Camarilla if they were just against the current Prince or something like that. If you so much as <i>accept</i> that the city has a Prince or Primogen and the Six Traditions, you're Camarilla, that's it. And from their part, the Camarilla doesn't accept members, it <i>assumes</i> it's universal among vampires. While it does have a few global or regional institutions, it was more an idea than an organization.<br /> <br /> Justicars are one of those few institutions, and almost the only one that affects nightly life, and they're a political appointment. So if one Justicar leaves the position... you just appoint a new one, as long as there's a single vampire in the clan who accepts the role, it can be done.<br /> <br /> For the Gangrel being Camarilla was just a matter of other people saying they're in and they having no reason to argue the point, plus there being enough clan members who actually gave a fuck to become Justicars, Primogen and stuff. Leaving was actually a very involved effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gangrel leaving the Camarilla never really made sense to me because it doesn't seem to help any of the Gangrel. What traditions do they stop following? Where do they go? What is the actual purpose other than a big tantrum about giving up their representation? How does this affect Gangrel in the Camarilla and PCs? The Gangrel and Brujah joining the Anarchs as Clans at least have a alternative to the Camarilla for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T18:37:37-08:00","id":1555697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555677#post1555677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My preferred headcanon outcome for Gehenna was always one where these very primitive creatures turn out not to be the great schemers that that they're thought to be, and that the world just goes on after they cancel one another out.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal headcanon is that most of them don't actually give a fuck, they're far more interested in small projects with little resemblance to the legends their clans (and players) tell about them.<br /> <br /> That has a lot to do with my personal take that the myths are far more important by themselves than the reality behind. Myths matter because people act on them, they learns from them, they take them as literal gospel. They also change them for various reasons, and those changes carry on and produce their own consequences. In this sense, the notion of the myths being real actually gets in my way in my chronicles than really help in any way, as it creates a kind of pressure to define &quot;The Truth\u2122&quot; that just messes with my game.<br /> <br /> So I prefer the Kindred myths to be seriously misguided. They have a kernel of truth, but as a direct telling of what happened they missed the point completely. When this truth, or part of it, is revealed for any reason, it looks nothing like what the myths say. Also because myths are generally the result of millennia of retellings and conflations, so even the actual people told about in them can't easily recognize the story or how it came to be.<br /> <br /> Just imagine a chronicle where the players are vampire archaeologists hunting down artifacts and texts and whatnot about an Ante, learning a complex tangle of contradicting stories and secrets, only to find out in the end their true patron was the Ante itself all along trying to piece together how the fuck their name came to be associated to a tale with so little resemblance to anything that ever happened.<br /> <br /> Also I tend not to have the Antes in torpor if they're at all relevant to a game. They're mostly awaken and aware and doing whatever they want. Which once you have such incredible powers... isn't really much, because why bother? I have a take with them very similar to what <i>Lair of the Hidden</i> did to the Inconnu in Hunedoara, personal feelings and small projects are far more relevant in their lives as they're mostly free from existential threats due to their immense power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555680#post1555680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel leaving the Camarilla never really made sense to me because it doesn't seem to help any of the Gangrel. What traditions do they stop following? Where do they go? What is the actual purpose other than a big tantrum about giving up their representation? How does this affect Gangrel in the Camarilla and PCs? The Gangrel and Brujah joining the Anarchs as Clans at least have a alternative to the Camarilla for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but I'm avoiding direct confrontation in this particular thread. If a player loves this lore change, well, that's it, I'll just explain whatever seems to have not been understood.<br /> <br /> But on top of all that, I especially find it baffling that the clan as a whole would follow the lead of their Justicar, because that's just not how the Gangrel work. They have no leadership, no united purpose. The decision of this guy may even convince a lot of members, but has no meaning for the clan as a whole, has no bearing on what they do. It was like if in the US the two senators of a given state declared their state was out of the Union and renounced their positions, and somehow that meant no one else can occupy their seats and the state is forever without senators despite nothing else changing (except half the population of the state went on a mass migration to Whatever Land, but for the other half nothing changes).\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T23:45:08-08:00","id":1555709,"title":"","content":"This part was truly amusing<br /> Clans are not countries nor have a governing bodies most of the time<br /> <br /> Even the highly organized Venture are more of a coalition of Dynasties descended from the kids od the Antediluvian and connected by &quot;royal&quot; Blood than a real power<br /> Even the Gerousia with all of its Praetor, the Aediles, the Questors and the &quot;rest&quot;, the Eiren is just\u2026 the Ventrues of a given locality<br /> Maybe - and this is a strong maybe - the Dignitas, the internal system of clan prestige for the Ventrue what matters to them<br /> <br /> Sure, the Gangrel have their own thing<br /> The aptly-named Gather, which are occasional meetings at which local and visiting Gangrel can exchange news, information and stories and decide on local matters<br /> Revels, which are essentially calls to battle.<br /> And of course the Great Gathers but they are extremely rare<br /> Even more rare but related are Grand Revels, which are essentially wars and battles involving the entire clan<br /> But these are rare because they relies on a powerful Gangrel who is respected by most of the clan and even then the main &quot;event&quot; is to establish the hierarchy before the business at hand can be dealt with.<br /> And even the Great Gather is... basically a meeting of all the local Gangrel in a given region.<br /> Not really a Global thing, especially not in the 20th or 21st century<br /> <br /> And the Camarilla as many pointed out is an idea<br /> A very young idea to be honest, but at the end of the day, just an idea - not necessarily a good idea, especially in the eyes of those who lived during the DA era and experienced the Vampire domains and courts and how darn effective they were<br /> The Camarilla is just an excuse maintaining order involve enacting the Traditions with a pragmatic view on Humanity<br /> You have the Inner Circle, sure, and their Justicars and their Archon assistants\u2026 but lets be real here, it is not about respect, it is not about honor<br /> It is simply fear<br /> The Justicars cultivate terror - they are of great age and power, and their ferocity is unparalleled<br /> Few can stand against them<br /> Like with the Princes, who are able to keep their domains because they had the resurces and power to establish themselves on the top (or someone with similar background and talent put them there) the Camarilla's rule is based on mostly a very primal and tribal thing: I am the strongest, get the hell out or bow your head before I destroy you<br /> <br /> Cool<br /> On local level it Works... mostly, but not really<br /> But on a global scale? Eh, not that much<br /> <br /> So the Gangrel - somehow - managed to decide, okay the Clan Will leave the Camarilla<br /> On local and personal level?<br /> Nobody gives a fuck, except for political rasons the Gangrel rarely bother with<br /> A Prince will not throw out an usefull Gangrel and a Gangrel suddenly will not pack and leave because the Clan is not Camarilla anymore<br /> A Gangrel power, influence, amassed status in the city and so on, like with every vampire, it is not based on the Camarilla or memebership - they are personal achivements (and personal power to hold on what you managed to claw out for yourself)<br /> <br /> Why a Vampire needs a Domain?<br /> For the purpose of feeding and asserting his will.<br /> And if you are strong enough you can allow others to feed and have their little playgrounds where they can assert their Will, as long as they Will obey your rule and come when you call them<br /> The older vampires remember fondly the time where the borders were drawn with the blood of the enemy, but for the younger ones it means if you are a bad boy you will end up on the business end of a stake or claw and it is game over maaaan<br /> In a Society that built on Boons ans Favors this primal fear ans show of power what keeps the cities working<br /> You can call it anything you want<br /> So it boils down to the personal level and many Gangrel probably not bothered to be called Camarilla members to begin with nor bothered now they are not members<br /> If the Prince wants something from you, he will enforce his will one way or a nother, twist your arm, send his goons, call in a few favors or offer you a boon\u2026 regardless of your sect membership<br /> Hell if it not gets out you could be a Sabbat chillin' in the city or a quiet Baali studing local demons, as long as you are usefull and have a good working relationship with someone powerfull (e.g. the Prince for example) nobody gives a shit - just don't rack the boat<br /> Thats it<br /> <br /> It is truly amusing in such a setup they made a big deal about the Gangrel &quot;leaving&quot; or others joining<br /> It baically only means they don't have a big scary vampire to assert his will in the name of the Inner Circles and his lackeys but another clan who joined filled this soci-ecological niche<br /> On city or personal level?<br /> Yeah basically means nothing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T23:49:46-08:00","id":1555710,"title":"","content":"I understand and don't wish to torpedo my own positive thread with negativity, though I certainly think it's possible to discsuss the positives the same way we discuss the negatives in this one's sister thread, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>.<br /> <br /> While barely touched upon, I like RECKONING OF NEW YORK's implication that Ravana is not necessarily dead. While it's a bit cheap that Lasombra, Tzimisce, and now Ravnos are apparently dead but not (Augustus Giovanni is seemingly the only &quot;truly&quot; dead Antediluvian alongside Cappadocias--and the fact there is no Beckoning implies that this is the case), I like the idea that Antediluvians just aren't capable of being killed the normal way one would do it.<br /> <br /> In my home games, I had a big revelation that Antediluvians are not long lived. They are indeed actually completely immortal and will always return from death until either God or Caine undoes their curse. Lucifer might also be able to do it. Diablerie is a way you can SORT OF kill them but inevitably their soul would take you over.<br /> <br /> Which means that players who want to play in Antediluvian games are best to try to just talk them down (which is possible in my games--oddly they are more likely to listen PCs than they are their fellow ancients for the sheer novelty of an ant colony spelling your name) or continue to make sure they sleep.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvians come from a time that is just different from Earth's present even if it's not Exalted. One of the other things that the PCs discovered was that Mithras wasn't a vampire impersonating a god.<br /> <br /> No, he was actually a Sun God embraced by Ventrue and so cursed. Which permanently cursed a large chunk of the Earth as a result. Because that's the way things worked way back when.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T01:02:23-08:00","id":1555713,"title":"","content":"I can definitely imagine the antediluvian of a clan that specializes in Fortitude as well as illusions playing possum and pretending to burn to ash. It's at least as plausible as the &quot;how can we ever be sure we killed a monster that could rewrite our memories&quot; idea that Clanbook: Lasombra Revised leaned so hard into.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, both scenarios involve an antediluvian who's famous for developing a special and flashy power, but really getting by on a high degree of development with a power that any elder would take for granted (Fortitude in one case, and Dominate in the other.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 11-26-2025, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T04:00:16-08:00","id":1555751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade#post1555518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, it's an odd title.<br /> <br /> POSITIVITY?<br /> <br /> But yes, sometimes retcons and changes to the game actually work out really well versus the opposite. Say what you will about Ur-Shulgi but the worst NPC in the history of the gameline was also effective for doing what was a massive boon to the game and that was facilitating the end of the &quot;Murder Cannibal Terrorist&quot; take on the Assamites/Banu Haqim.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the Schism, too. I miss the castes, though, and would have focused on the breadth of castes in Revised/V20, while adding some new ones. But then again, I think most clans would benefit from castes as recognised clan variants that aren't fully independent bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade#post1555518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ravnos have been revised three or four times and each time for the better. So much so that I actually think the 5th Edition versions are the best of them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I might agree, although their clan bane is potentially too much. Though, again, I did like the panoply of jati they had before, as they provided more of a framework to tie your ideas to. I just think they needed to step away from real-life Indian social strata (and casteism), and again make them broader.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same for the Tzimisce as I think there's far more room with &quot;Dragons in Human Form who rule over their feudal apartment building and consider everything in their hordes&quot; than there is with fleshcrafting Necroscope vampires who are just alien and evil because. </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Both seem as narrow as each other to me. Now allowing for both to exist simultaneously? Well, now that's more like it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade#post1555518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OPP was no stranger to this themselves and I loved how they handled virtually every single plot idea in BJD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. On the bloodlines front, I really liked what they hinted at for the Tremere antitribu and Blood Brothers, as well as the bloodlines in general. The Montreal/Sabbat civil war stuff was also a real highlight.<br /> <br /> Other additions I liked? I kinda really liked the Black Monastery in the Giovanni Chronicles, because it foregrounds the Sabbat as a spiritual organisation, and this became the basis, in my games, for the sect to become a haven for those who refused to give up their Roads, as well as those who were more overtly occultist.<br /> <br /> That's always been there, but the Black Monastery was where it &quot;clicked&quot; for me, and made me realise that the Sabbat needed more infrastructure for this stuff. Montreal also has these small shrines to each of the major Paths inside the Temple of Night, but these aren't really mentioned anywhere else. But they really speak to the Paths as religions.<br /> <br /> So I invented stuff like Black Cathedrals\u2014hidden sites around the world where Path paragons congregate to set the spiritual direction of the sect\u2014and Seminaries, where said paragons teach pack priests. At the local level, different Paths would also have shrines for worship. And the most devoted Path members would probably get inducted into the &quot;mysteries&quot; behind the Path, effectively resembling the Roads but even more secretive. (Sort of like the way Tibetan Buddhism teaches the Mahayana to everyone, but those who are initiated also get to do all the cool Vajrayana stuff that turbo-charges your practice.)<br /> <br /> What else? I liked some of the weird shit in first edition, such as the succubus in Chicago by Night, because they suggest a World of Darkness in which things don't always work the way we expect. Is she a minor Fallen? A type of fae? Just a spirit?<br /> <br /> V5 does some of this, too, such as with Aapilu, but probably folds too much of it back into an explicitly vampiric, blood-based cosmology. I much prefer Aapilu as just one type of possible demonic entity you might encounter, alongside whatever the Children are, whatever Kupala is, whatever the Lilim are, etc.<br /> <br /> In general, though, I favour anything that gives us more cool stuff and more options, as you can probably tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T17:19:50-08:00","id":1555815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555751#post1555751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Schism, too. I miss the castes, though, and would have focused on the breadth of castes in Revised/V20</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they remove the castes in V5?<br /> <br /> The Schism comes from <i>Revised</i>'s <i>Clanbook: Assamite</i>, and they kept the castes, there. My only problem was with the idea of almost the entire Warrior caste becoming the Web of Knifes and then betraying the clan for Ur-Shulgi (yes, for me that was betrayal). I'd much prefer to have all three castes represented in both sides in numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555751#post1555751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, again, I did like the panoply of jati they had before, as they provided more of a framework to tie your ideas to. I just think they needed to step away from real-life Indian social strata (and casteism), and again make them broader.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they could be broader as mechanics go, but the concept actually works.<br /> <br /> Not because I think it's a good idea to make a fictional allegory to each Jati, but because I like the idea of your life as a mortal carrying into your life as a Vampire, so they keep understanding themselves as members of their Jati and acting accordingly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555751#post1555751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. Both seem as narrow as each other to me. Now allowing for both to exist simultaneously? Well, now that's more like it!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I usually do, although I vehemently disagree they're just as narrow, if for no other reason because the Old Clan has far less pressure for everyone to behave like that, at most you have to follow the hospitality rules because you're in fact required to, not because you're innately wired to like them.<br /> <br /> What happens with the <i>Necroscope-</i>like standard Tzimisce is that for their strangeness to work, the book heavily imply a similar <i>Necroscope</i> situation where everyone is a super-sadistic alien with an incomprehensible mind. You <i>can</i> technically deviate from it, but it's way more visible and possibly problematic both within the setting and with the themes.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555751#post1555751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other additions I liked? I kinda really liked the Black Monastery in the Giovanni Chronicles, because it foregrounds the Sabbat as a spiritual organisation, and this became the basis, in my games, for the sect to become a haven for those who refused to give up their Roads, as well as those who were more overtly occultist.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I didn't read the Giovanni Chronicles, I do like this take a lot and have been using it for a time to great effect.<br /> <br /> Currently my Sabbat is less about wanton violence (although there <i>are</i> plenty packs that practice it) and more about mysticism and religion, spirituality, and exploring the meaning of vampirism instead of just living it safely(-ish).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555751#post1555751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked some of the weird shit in first edition, such as the succubus in Chicago by Night</div> </div> </div> </div>I do this as frequent as I can. My players find a lot of things they can't easily categorize just with setting knowledge. There are things that simply don't conform to any particular world view or anyone's knowledge of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T08:21:59-08:00","id":1555826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555680#post1555680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel leaving the Camarilla never really made sense to me because it doesn't seem to help any of the Gangrel. What traditions do they stop following? Where do they go? What is the actual purpose other than a big tantrum about giving up their representation? How does this affect Gangrel in the Camarilla and PCs? The Gangrel and Brujah joining the Anarchs as Clans at least have a alternative to the Camarilla for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing here was because the Camarilla denied the Antediluvians and Xaviar, being the Justicar at that time, fought what he believed was an Antediluvian (again, this was a yes and no situation). He was so pissed off that the elders disregarded his claims that he took the entire clan out, and his political position allowed him to back up his claim. Many left, out of respect for the elder, but many remained. All this background is on Clan Novel Gangrel, it's really good.<br /> <br /> For the Brujah I'd like more on this, I don't know if the Convention of Prague is covered in any V5 book since it's very sketchy on Camarilla and Anarch sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T06:02:17-08:00","id":1555847,"title":"","content":"To be honest, the Clan Gangrel doing a walk-out from the Camarilla would work best if it were contextualised as the Clan making it plain that they work <i>with</i> the Camarilla, they do not work <i>for</i> the Ivory Tower: this being not necessarily intended as a permenant state of affairs but as a Power Move to demonstrate Gangrel self-sufficiency and demonstrate that the Camarilla is useful, but not so overwhelmingly essential that it can simply dictate terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T06:08:58-08:00","id":1555848,"title":"","content":"Almost forgot to add: given that the Gangrel have a long association with self-sufficiency, it\u2019s interesting that we don\u2019t have many examples of Gangrel observing a great deal of historic fuss and bother, then walking away to calmly go about their own business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T07:50:47-08:00","id":1555850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555826#post1555826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing here was because the Camarilla denied the Antediluvians and Xaviar, being the Justicar at that time, fought what he believed was an Antediluvian (again, this was a yes and no situation). He was so pissed off that the elders disregarded his claims that he took the entire clan out, and his political position allowed him to back up his claim. Many left, out of respect for the elder, but many remained. All this background is on Clan Novel Gangrel, it's really good.<br /> <br /> For the Brujah I'd like more on this, I don't know if the Convention of Prague is covered in any V5 book since it's very sketchy on Camarilla and Anarch sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>THE CAMARILLA covered it with essentially the Inner Council expelling the Brujah after so many high ranking members helped Theo Bell escape (which apparently he hadn't planned on). It also introduced the Hellenes as those Brujah who were allowed to remain without a representative.<br /> <br /> It's implied something happened to the Brujah Inner Councilwoman too (not the Beckoning) but I honestly forget what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-02T04:43:53-08:00","id":1556093,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with the Brujah being expelled from the Camarilla. They were always more of an Anarch clan anyway. And I like that the Hellenes (Idealists) were allowed to remain. They were always the more moderate clan members anyway, who advocated for peaceful change within the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-11T05:50:00-08:00","id":1557468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555657#post1555657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I love Camarilla Lasombra, but I do agree that defection plot had some issues.<br /> <br /> In large part, because it isn\u2019t cool. The Lasombra came to the Camarilla on their knees, humbling themselves. That isn\u2019t their style. That isn\u2019t cool.<br /> <br /> That is why I would rather the Lasombra gain enough power to demand full status within the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not only that, but by sacrificing their elders, the Lasombra were basically neutering their own clan. They're killing off the lower generation members to cozy up to the Ivory Tower, which means all the Lasombra going forward will be higher generation trash with few prospects of moving up the ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T05:45:03-08:00","id":1557504,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra are suffering the Beckoning as much as anyone else so the promise to sacrifice &quot;Elders&quot; isn't a huge one anyway. But I stated that the Lasombra were going to have kill a bunch of their people on the way out anyway so it was a &quot;I was going to do this thing anyway&quot; sort of clause.<br /> <br /> Lots of people disagree with my interpretation, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T08:55:10-08:00","id":1557509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1557468#post1557468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not only that, but by sacrificing their elders, the Lasombra were basically neutering their own clan. They're killing off the lower generation members to cozy up to the Ivory Tower, which means all the Lasombra going forward will be higher generation trash with few prospects of moving up the ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The letter of the deal was not to deliver elders of the Lasombra, but elders of the Sabbat.<br /> This is actually important<br /> Also individual Princes are enforcing their own Lasombra admittance rules <br /> Not to mention at the end of the day Amici Noctis decides which Lasombra are exempt from the internal hunt<br /> <br /> So actually it is more of strengthening of the Clan and weeding out the <i>faliures</i> who lack the survival instinct to let go the &quot;Sabbat Project&quot; thus proved themselves to be unworthy to be Lasombra<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T09:14:37-08:00","id":1557512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1557468#post1557468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not only that, but by sacrificing their elders, the Lasombra were basically neutering their own clan. They're killing off the lower generation members to cozy up to the Ivory Tower, which means all the Lasombra going forward will be higher generation trash with few prospects of moving up the ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its also worth noting that they've re-established the pre revolt hierachy and culture....the one that failed and blew up in their faces when the anarch revolt kicked off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1557509#post1557509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The letter of the deal was not to deliver elders of the Lasombra, but elders of the Sabbat.<br /> This is actually important<br /> Also individual Princes are enforcing their own Lasombra admittance rules<br /> Not to mention at the end of the day Amici Noctis decides which Lasombra are exempt from the internal hunt<br /> <br /> So actually it is more of strengthening of the Clan and weeding out the <i>faliures</i> who lack the survival instinct to let go the &quot;Sabbat Project&quot; thus proved themselves to be unworthy to be Lasombra</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats arguably worse in terms of attrition. Trying to capture loyalist lasombra (who outnumber you) is difficult enough without drawing the other clan/bloodlines in.<br /> <br /> And thats before we consider the princes who are smart enough that their 'admittance policy' is &quot;lol no.&quot; In some variety.<br /> <br /> it definatly doesnt strengthen the clan, thats just lasombra coping about an embarrising surrender since social darwinism is nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-12-2026, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T09:28:29-08:00","id":1557513,"title":"","content":"QUOTE=GreatHornedRatkin;n1557468] <br /> <br /> Not only that, but by sacrificing their elders, the Lasombra were basically neutering their own clan. They're killing off the lower generation members to cozy up to the Ivory Tower, which means all the Lasombra going forward will be higher generation trash with few prospects of moving up the ranks.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Its also worth noting that they've re-established the pre revolt hierachy and culture....the one that failed and blew up in their faces when the anarch revolt kicked off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1557509#post1557509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The letter of the deal was not to deliver elders of the Lasombra, but elders of the Sabbat.<br /> This is actually important<br /> Also individual Princes are enforcing their own Lasombra admittance rules<br /> Not to mention at the end of the day Amici Noctis decides which Lasombra are exempt from the internal hunt<br /> <br /> So actually it is more of strengthening of the Clan and weeding out the faliures who lack the survival instinct to let go the &quot;Sabbat Project&quot; thus proved themselves to be unworthy to be Lasombra</div> </div> </div> </div> Thats arguably worse in terms of attrition. Trying to capture loyalist lasombra (who outnumber you) is difficult enough without drawing the other clan/bloodlines in.<br /> <br /> And thats before we consider the princes who are smart enough that their 'admittance policy' is &quot;lol no.&quot; In some variety.<br /> <br /> it definatly doesnt strengthen the clan, thats just lasombra coping about an embarrising surrender since social darwinism is nonsense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T09:51:15-08:00","id":1557514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1557509#post1557509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So actually it is more of strengthening of the Clan and weeding out the <i>faliures</i> who lack the survival instinct to let go the &quot;Sabbat Project&quot; thus proved themselves to be unworthy to be Lasombra</div> </div> </div> </div>Refusing to accept defeat and clawing your way back to prominence is exactly what the screening process for becoming Lasombra entails.<br /> <br /> By abandoning the Swords of Caine and begging the Camarilla to take them in, it is the defectors who prove themselves unworthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T09:57:39-08:00","id":1557515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555518-what-lore-changes-did-you-love-added-to-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1557513#post1557513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">QUOTE=GreatHornedRatkin;n1557468]<br /> <br /> Thats arguably worse in terms of attrition. Trying to capture loyalist lasombra (who outnumber you) is difficult enough without drawing the other clan/bloodlines in.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I'm not sure the Sabbat Lasombra outnumber the non-Sabbat Lasombra<br /> More like the other way around actually<br /> If you look at the factions:<br /> <br /> The<b> Corsairs</b> (Lasombra that have answered the call of the sea that seems to be inherent to their blood. They spend most of their time on the waves, often masquerading as pirates, and some never come on dry land) are never really been Sabbat or only a handfull of joined, they were independent or nominally Sabbat at best. Not Camarilla or not numerous in the Camarilla either but Alfonso L\u00f3pez for example was an infamous Lasombra antitribu Pirate, renowned for his naval strikes against the Sabbat tho' he has been seen lastly in the 1960s<br /> <br /> The <b>Faithful</b> (Lasombra who draw their traditions from the once strong hold of the Lasombra within the Catholic Church. Ardent followers of God and believers in their own damnation alike, these individuals seek to fulfill the will of God in this world) I think had presence everywhere. Mon\u00e7ada is a good example<br /> <br /> <b>The Kings and Queens of Shadow</b>, Lasombra who took part in mortal institutions, exerting influence, gathering resources and in general keeping the mortal population unaware of the vampires among them always distanced themselves from regular Sabbat activities to maintain their Humanity. They were nominally Sabbat or not at all<br /> <br /> <b>The Children of the Abyss, </b>the Lasombra<b>, </b>whofollowed the ancient traditions of Abyss Mysticism payed only lip service to the Sabbat as the sect provides them with the means to pursue their arcane art.<br /> <br /> <b>The Transhumanists, </b>Lasombra who revel in their predatory nature and seek to perfect their undead state are a puzzling wlyd card since they quantify their various powers, work out taxonomies and otherwise seek to reduce vampirism to data. Many have a keen interest in mortal technology, particular in those that augment the human body, while others seek a perfect state without reliance on external tools. To be fair the Sabbat at best was an interesting experiment to catalog to them in my humble oppinion, not something they followed faithfully<br /> <br /> <b>The Fatalists</b> are those Lasombra that have stopped believing in freedom of Will. Many claim that their blood ties them directly to the elders and methuselahs of their Clan and these beings are in charge of the destinies of their progeny - this is everything the Sabbat is not. And more of a Camarilla thing...<br /> <br /> <b>The Doomed </b>were the exhibitionist lot among the Clan that do not believe in the value of secrecy and aimed to gain immediate and direct control of their environment, often without concerns to the kine. Many Lasombra killed those Clan mates on sight. They are... I don't know to be honest. But already member who had a target on their head<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Angels</b> also called Angellis Ater were the Lasombra who reveled in their state as servants of Satan and enemies of God, practicing Satanism and other socially repulsive things. Infernalist more often than not. Not something the Sabbat tolerated. Neither the Camarilla for that matter. Or you know, anyone else with a working braincell - Baali wanabees<br /> <br /> The only who were truly Sabbat if you ask me, wete the <b>Crusaders</b> who viewed the Sabbat as a religious and military organization almost to the exclusion of the Sabbat as an ideology of freedom.<br /> <br /> Then you had the &quot;real&quot; <b>Lasombra <i>antitribu </i></b>or a faction led by Montano who already had a cozy place in the Cammarila and the <b>Qabilat al-Khayal </b>the Lasombra of the Ashirra<br /> And if you want to go a mile, Clan Lasombra Trilogy 2: Shadows mentions Khanom Mehr, childe of the Lasombra Antediluvian whose name is possible Persian, Indian or Thai origin and many belive the Lasombra from the East toward Asia are likely descendants of her.<br /> <br /> So all and all?<br /> I don't think the Clan as a whole was Sabbat to begin with, or loyal to the Sabbat and not jumping boat as soon as anything remotely interesting or better presented itself except the <b>Crusaders</b>\u200b and lets say half of the <b>Faithful</b> and maybe some <b>Doomed</b> ?\u200b<br /> <br /> Of course it is just my interpretation but I think holds up<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-12T10:00:35-08:00","id":1557516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div clas