ct control of their environment, often without concerns to the kine. Many Lasombra killed those Clan mates on sight. They are... I don't know to be honest. But already member who had a target on their head<br /> <br /> <b>The Black Angels</b> also called Angellis Ater were the Lasombra who reveled in their state as servants of Satan and enemies of God, practicing Satanism and other socially repulsive things. Infernalist more often than not. Not something the Sabbat tolerated. Neither the Camarilla for that matter. Or you know, anyone else with a working braincell - Baali wanabees<br /> <br /> The only who were truly Sabbat if you ask me, wete the <b>Crusaders</b> who viewed the Sabbat as a religious and military organization almost to the exclusion of the Sabbat as an ideology of freedom.<br /> <br /> Then you had the &quot;real&quot; <b>Lasombra <i>antitribu </i></b>or a faction led by Montano who already had a cozy place in the Cammarila and the <b>Qabilat al-Khayal </b>the Lasombra of the Ashirra<br /> And if you want to go a mile, Clan Lasombra Trilogy 2: Shadows mentions Khanom Mehr, childe of the Lasombra Antediluvian whose name is possible Persian, Indian or Thai origin and many belive the Lasombra from the East toward Asia are likely descendants of her.<br /> <br /> So all and all?<br /> I don't think the Clan as a whole was Sabbat to begin with, or loyal to the Sabbat and not jumping boat as soon as anything remotely interesting or better presented itself except the <b>Crusaders</b> and lets say half of the <b>Faithful</b> and maybe some <b>Doomed</b> ?\u200b<br /> <br /> Of course it is just my interpretation but I think holds up<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They explicitly do, dawkin commented on in his video on them its something like 40/30/30 sect ratio<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/miE5B4hCmOY?s